.TH pagesize 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
pagesize \- print the memory page size
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pagesize
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pagesize
prints the size in bytes of the unit the kernel allocates memory in.
.SH NOTES
FUZIX does not page.  A process is a single contiguous run of memory,
swapped out whole and back in whole; the number here is the granularity
of that allocation, not the size of a virtual memory page.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR free (1),
.BR ps (1)
